---
kind: handoff
ext: .handoff
version: 1
mime: application/x-handoff
binary: false
trigger: handoff pick up where you left off continue this chat
---

## Purpose

A handoff is the unit another chat needs to continue a job. It carries a paste block and a file list. A note without files is not a handoff.

## Structure

1. Line 1 is the magic banner `# handoff v1`
2. A YAML block between `---` fences with keys mission, continue_from, stop_rule
3. A `FILES` section, one path per line
4. A `PASTE` section, the exact text the next chat must receive
5. A `RULES` section, one `KEY: value` per line

## Parse rules

- Reject the file if line 1 is not `# handoff v1`
- Read mission, continue_from, and stop_rule from the fenced block
- FILES lines are paths. Blank lines are ignored
- PASTE is raw text until the next section heading
- RULES split on the first `: `
- A handoff with an empty FILES list is invalid
- A handoff with an empty PASTE section is invalid

## Write rules

- Always start with `# handoff v1`
- Name the body to continue, not a summary of the ticks
- List only files the next chat must open
- Put the paste block in PASTE, verbatim
- Do not claim a tick continued unless the stop_rule test passed

